# clang-tidy checks for zash. clangd (run with --clang-tidy) reads
# this file, so the editor shows the same findings as a manual run
# (`make compdb` first, for compile_commands.json):
#   clang-tidy -p . *.c libedit/port/*.c
#
# libedit/netbsd/ is vendored upstream code; libedit/netbsd/.clang-tidy
# turns every check off there.
#
# Disabled on purpose:
#   readability-magic-numbers          signal numbers, exit statuses (126,
#                                      127, 128+n) and fd 0-2 are the
#                                      readable form
#   readability-identifier-length      short names (lx, t, p) are the
#                                      house style
#   readability-braces-around-statements
#   readability-isolate-declaration    style choices, not bugs
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#                                      the lexer and evaluator are flat
#                                      switches
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion
#                                      a C++ check: in C the language
#                                      itself promotes bool to int in
#                                      &&, ||, ! and ?:, so every bool
#                                      condition is flagged (newer
#                                      clang-tidy applies it to C)
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#                                      too noisy for small helpers
#   cert-err33-c                       unchecked printf/fputs results
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#                                      suggests C11 Annex K (fprintf_s),
#                                      which glibc and z/OS don't ship
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
# zash's own headers (shell.h, libedit/port/*.h), not vendored ones
HeaderFilterRegex: '(^|/)(shell\.h|libedit/port/.*\.h)$'
